Naughty Dog's long-awaited sequel The  Last of Us part two is finally out in  the wild here are seven spoiler free  tips to give you an edge as you fight  your way through this cruel and violent  world number one looting and crafting  looting is a big part of the last of us  as gameplay loop in between each  encounter you should be scanning the  environment look for drawers cupboards  and other compartments as you clear  abandoned buildings and rusted out cars  as you Luke you'll find supplies which  you can use to craft things like arrows  explosives and explosive arrows the  amount of supplies you can find will  directly coincide with the difficulty  you choose if you pick easy you'll find  plenty of crafting parts and if you  choose survivor you probably won't find  many if you picked an easier difficulty  you'll probably run out of space often  so make sure you craft things as  frequently as possible if you're playing  survivor crafts wisely if you ever feel  as though you're under prepared or over  prepared for fire fights we recommend  adjusting the difficulty because you can  do so at any time number two difficulty  and accessibility speaking of difficulty  The Last of Us part two has a ton of  difficulty and accessibility options for  you to tweak and manipulate to your  heart's content you can adjust the enemy  AI the amount of resources you can find  the damage the player takes and how  capable your allies are you can even go  into the accessibility options and  further tweak the gameplay to suit your  play style number three collectibles  Naughty Dog love's collectibles and the  Last of Us part two is no different  collectibles come in many forms  including artifacts trading cards and  journal entries artifacts mostly consist  of notes that add flavor to the area you  are exploring trading cards are cards  that Ellie is into and journal entries  are things in the environment that Ellie  will sketch if you interact with it most  collectibles can only be found in  non-combat areas however there are a few  exceptions the most notable one is  hidden under a bed in the Hillcrest  section so keep your eyes peeled if  you're a completionist we recommend  turning on high contrast mode and  enhance listen mode in the accessibility  menu high contrast mode will highlight  things in your environment you can  interact with by swiping the touchpad  and enhance listening mode will ping  nearby items number for safes as you  explore the world you'll also come  across locked combination safes these  safes contain training manuals which  unlock new skills new weapons and of  course extra  on supplies if you find a safe it's in  your best interest to crack it to do  that you'll need to find the combination  somewhere in the environment many can be  found on letters left behind however  there are a few trickier ones that  require you to survey the environment  carefully the combination will almost  always be close to the safe itself  number five bricks and bottles break  bones now that we have that out of the  way let's talk about combat part twos  combat is fast tense and difficult if  you aren't prepared if you find yourself  low on ammo or supplies look for bricks  or bottles in the environment not only  can you use them to distract enemies but  a well-thrown bottle or brick can also  stun an enemy serving them up for an  easy kill  this can be clutched on harder  difficulties when supplies and ammo are  scarce number six dogs new to the last  of us are dogs as much as it pains me to  kill these not-so-good boys it is in  your best interest to dispatch them  quickly if a dog catches your scent it  will follow it until it finds you or  loses the trail you can see your scent  by holding our one to activate listen  mode a good way to take care of a dog on  your trail is by placing a tripmine  eventually the dog will get close enough  to set it off and I wouldn't recommend  looking that direction when it does if  you'd rather do with them non lethally a  well-thrown brick or bottle can also  throw them off your scent number seven  run  [Music]  just like in The Last of Us one you can  run from most encounters if you're  spotted while you're trying to stealth  through an area you can run out of the  enemy's line-of-sight and reposition  yourself or you can simply try to run to  the next area if you play on the  survivor difficulty setting running is a  totally viable option that will help you  conserve your precious ammo those are  seven tips that should help you stay  alive in the last of us part two if you  have any other things you'd like to add  leave them in the comments below and  we'll see you next time  you
 

